error[E0277]: a borrowed container of `i64` has no storage of its own type: the container's storage holds the runtime's values, not `i64`s
  --> tests/compile_fail/in_place_read_of_a_converted_element.rs:14:15
   |
14 |     unsafe { <Vec<i64> as Borrowable<Rt>>::deref(rt, reference) }.len()
   |               ^^^^^^^^ this parameter borrows a container of `i64`
   |
   = help: the trait `InPlaceElement<Rt>` is not implemented for `i64`
   = note: borrow the elements as a slice: the language's `&[i64]` and `&mut [i64]` are taken as `Slice<Erased<Rt, i64>, Shared, Rt>` and `Slice<Erased<Rt, i64>, Mut, Rt>`, whose elements read in place as `i64` by `as_ref(rt)` and `as_mut(rt)` where `i64: Stored<Rt>`; a `i64` that is itself `TransparentOver<Rt>`, as an `Erased<Rt, X>` is, is taken as `Slice<i64, Shared, Rt>` and `Slice<i64, Mut, Rt>` (RFC-0047).
   = note: a `Vec<i64>` taken by value materializes each element, and an `async` declaration may take one, which it may not a slice.
help: the trait `InPlaceElement<R>` is implemented for `Erased<R, T>`
  --> $WORKSPACE/acvus-extern/src/erased.rs
   |
   | / impl<R, T> InPlaceElement<R> for Erased<R, T>
   | | where
   | |     R: Runtime,
   | |     T: 'static,
   | |     Self: crate::Branded,
   | |_________________________^
   = note: required for `Vec<i64>` to implement `Borrowable<Rt>`

